&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Voyager team at Anduril Industries is an engineering and design division with vast experience in developing innovative computing and communications solutions for the network edge. We specialize in integrating enterprise networking capabilities from global IT leaders with purpose-built hardware and software platforms designed to meet the most stringent environmental requirements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a portion of the production quality support process for a certain product or set of products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct data analysis and data mining to identify trends and patterns in product quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain KPIs &amp;amp; OKR metrics to track product quality and identify areas for improvement and drive improvement through a cross-functional team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a project that transforms an element of the quality engineering team – a process, new inspection method, or complex data analytic method(s)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Will support Anduril’s quality management system and manage changes to documentation and training at the conclusion of the project&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write documentation required for successfully quality management for hardware at scale, such as work instructions, quality plans, inspection requirements, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with technicians and other engineers hands-on, building and measuring prototype hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possibly travel to suppliers to do initial sourcing work, solve ongoing production issues, and implement quality procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completion of a bachelors or masters degree in a technical field such as engineering, maths or science.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be available to work full time in our Dublin office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be available to start full time in July 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous internship experience within the quality production space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to creatively problem solve issues related electromechanical hardware in a resource-constrained environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated in-kind or direct team leadership skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal experience with inspection systems, data analysis, numeric methods, MatLab or other software packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in data analysis, process improvement, and thirst for learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience leading project and working with data collection, analysis, and driving improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software scripting experience in any language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be comfortable working in a lab environment using Power Supplies, Electronic Loads, Digital Volt Meters etc&lt;/li&gt;
