&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anduril is seeking a Classified DevSecOps Engineer who will be focused on Infrastructure as Code (IaC) for both on-premise and cloud deployments. You will be responsible for working with Cybersecurity, Systems Engineers, and Software Engineers, to develop next-generation computational, networking, and storage capabilities across the enterprise. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable, hybrid architectures that span across on-premise and cloud environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and test secure multi-tenant capabilities to allow consolidation of resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research, develop, and evaluate new technologies, both hardware and software, to meet customer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across multiple teams to build DevSecOps processes and establish Continuous Integration / Continuous Development (CI/CD) pipelines for automating Infrastructure and Policy as Code (IaC/PaC)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaison between the business lines and Program Management to capture requirements and propose solutions that meet their needs on time and on budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define baseline requirements and manage vendor relationships to include evaluation of proposals and development of Statements of Work (SOW) as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and lead other engineers &amp;amp; developers to grow the IaC skillset across the teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge and experience with Linux Operating Systems (OS) such as Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL), Rocky Linux, Ubuntu, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Infrastructure as Code (IaC) concepts and using automation &amp;amp; scripting tools such as Ansible, Terraform, Puppet, Chef, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of network switching &amp;amp; routing concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Agile development processes and understanding of GitOps leveraging Continuous Integration / Continuous Delivery (CI/CD) pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligible to obtain an maintain a US Top Secret Clearance with customer’s approval&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;May be required to obtain and maintain DoD 8140/8570 qualifying certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;DESIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with container orchestration, such as Kubernetes (k8s), and container runtimes (e.g. Podman, Docker, Shifter, AppTainer/Singularity, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Software Defined Networking (SDN) and leveraging service mesh&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Policy as Code (PaC) tools such as OPA, Oso, Cedar, Kyverno, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, GCP, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working Identity and Access Management (IDAM) solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with software development and debugging in one or more languages (e.g. Go, Rust, Python)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with core security concepts including encryption, authentication, identity and access management, and Zero-Trust Architecture (ZTA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of NIST SP 800-53 controls and their technical implementation to meet cybersecurity requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant certifications such as Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA), Linux+, LPIC-*, Red Hat Certified Administrator / Engineer (RHCSA/RHCSE), etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$142,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$188,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril&#39;s total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
