&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop system requirements and test campaigns for Anduril’s wide range of airbreathing turbine applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design test campaigns and development efforts to satisfy program feature requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with program and customer demands to deliver high quality propulsion products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with engine control systems including FADEC’s, ECU’s, Starter-Generators and related hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with actuators, sensors, connectors and architecture of engine control systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop test stands, instrumentation packages and equipment to support engine test and integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test, diagnose, and analyze engine data on test stands, on test expeditions, and in flight test.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on the coolest engines in the aviation business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical, Mechatronics Engineering, Aerospace Engineering or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years relevant engineering experience in gas turbine / aerospace / defense / automotive / passenger car / commercial vehicle industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding, and intuition for the physics of basic propulsion systems, motion control systems, and heat transfer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with engines, engine controls, and/or testing of engines or powertrain components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with verification test plan writing and execution, MIL standards, and feature development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate well with other electrical, mechanical, software, firmware, and test engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with diagnostics monitoring, failure detection and data analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be a U.S. Person due to required access to U.S. export controlled information or facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel time up to 25%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Masters or advanced degree in Mechanical, Aerospace, Mechatronics Engineering, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to assist with part selection, board design, and product design efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to assist with designing simple mechanical parts (CAD). Knowledge of manufacturing methods (machining, sheet metal, composites, 3D printing, injection molding, etc.) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in procuring development parts and working in a fabrication environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mechatronics experience; sensor selection, setup of data acquisition systems, assemble wire harnesses and debug/troubleshoot systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CANape or similar CAN interface tool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the design and implementation of automotive or aviation control electronics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience developing embedded systems for automotive or aviation powertrain controls is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
